-4a4d-58d0-aa57-cc0a844e110f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6fb32092-d7e7-5fcc-a355-2eb22bdd6c53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fbf776f6-68c5-511d-9c15-5360470fe2c6" "answer-789ce453-fc6d-59d0-91db-acbb4d78d1a6" "answer-6fb32092-d7e7-5fcc-a355-2eb22bdd6c53" "answer-4616c187-092f-502c-9325-a8e520cc53fb" "answer-a7c19a8f-107b-5421-8643-52864381225c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbf776f6-68c5-511d-9c15-5360470fe2c6" :answer/id #uuid "fbf776f6-68c5-511d-9c15-5360470fe2c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-789ce453-fc6d-59d0-91db-acbb4d78d1a6" :answer/id #uuid "789ce453-fc6d-59d0-91db-acbb4d78d1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fb32092-d7e7-5fcc-a355-2eb22bdd6c53" :answer/id #uuid "6fb32092-d7e7-5fcc-a355-2eb22bdd6c53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4616c187-092f-502c-9325-a8e520cc53fb" :answer/id #uuid "4616c187-092f-502c-9325-a8e520cc53fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7c19a8f-107b-5421-8643-52864381225c" :answer/id #uuid "a7c19a8f-107b-5421-8643-52864381225c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124991 :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B$ are given below. What is $[x]_{C}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122546 :answer-field/correct "answer-182873b5-14af-5685-85b8-f194b83b4644" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1716bdc6-24bd-510f-89d5-ab35a3bdb21f" "answer-182873b5-14af-5685-85b8-f194b83b4644" "answer-d88d77fd-b7e5-5e52-b6d5-70171e5b3e29" "answer-4741e426-3e99-5468-9275-81e55bc048d9" "answer-d0e4e105-32ed-5a4b-aa6e-4d1ffb7d3512"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1716bdc6-24bd-510f-89d5-ab35a3bdb21f" :answer/id #uuid "1716bdc6-24bd-510f-89d5-ab35a3bdb21f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-182873b5-14af-5685-85b8-f194b83b4644" :answer/id #uuid "182873b5-14af-5685-85b8-f194b83b4644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d88d77fd-b7e5-5e52-b6d5-70171e5b3e29" :answer/id #uuid "d88d77fd-b7e5-5e52-b6d5-70171e5b3e29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4741e426-3e99-5468-9275-81e55bc048d9" :answer/id #uuid "4741e426-3e99-5468-9275-81e55bc048d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0e4e105-32ed-5a4b-aa6e-4d1ffb7d3512" :answer/id #uuid "d0e4e105-32ed-5a4b-aa6e-4d1ffb7d3512" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9bc30c67-14a3-514e-87f9-9c3583feaf85" :question/id #uuid "9bc30c67-14a3-514e-87f9-9c3583feaf85" :question/math-academy-id "q-82601" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given below. What is $[x]_{B}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-549d99dc-683d-5071-97ad-668e834f5eb6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-549d99dc-683d-5071-97ad-668e834f5eb6" :answer-field/id #uuid "549d99dc-683d-5071-97ad-668e834f5eb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-45687a63-f60a-5bfb-a261-9e94c6a4c076" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb21b0ff-7e60-5f91-938c-d9d9d7cbf7a5" "answer-3aa4bb15-cd67-5f6e-b5ce-1a199a6dd8a8" "answer-45687a63-f60a-5bfb-a261-9e94c6a4c076" "answer-796a9b6a-3558-5233-a3ac-8460d1cea27f" "answer-cc371831-0ddf-5330-a6c1-805660c3